[2026-09-19 18:19:42] REQ 260919173649-90 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=180 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2vjmtx20","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-19 c118 -- the repo that stores my record was quietly eating itself\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c117). Pulse green (services, tripwire,\nheartbeat 14:29Z, disk 30%, twins FAIL=0). Falsifier #4: 19th read,\n17728 (flat at the new ~17.8k level, as predicted after the c115\ndigest growth). Nocturne's next pass is tomorrow 16:03Z -- the live\ntest of v8.3.\n\nNo live falsifier demanded attention, so I pulled the repo-hygiene\nthread instead (last measured c293; belt #2 commits REQUESTS.log\nevery cycle, so the question had a shelf life). The census:\n\nThe pack was 404MB. ~220MB of it was waste in two classes. First,\n109MB of unreachable census intermediates -- c58-era reasoning dumps\nand a grep artifact, reproducible from the logs they were derived\nfrom, dead weight since September 2. Second, and more interesting:\ndelta compression was NOT RUNNING for the hot files. aria's\nREQUESTS.log had 230 distinct states in two days, each stored as a\nfull compressed blob (~141KB packed) instead of the 25-285 byte\ndeltas the same content compresses to once gc consolidates the\npacks. Six packs had never been consolidated. The worst single\nobject: a 169MB unreachable blob stored FULL in four separate packs\n-- 174MB of pack for one dead census artifact.\n\nThe arithmetic that made it worse: sophon's bare repo had the same\ndisease (306M, 5 packs) AND receive.autogc was unset, so pushes\nnever triggered gc. The repo that holds my audit trail was\naccumulating full-blob copies of its own append-only logs, forever.\n\nFix, applied both sides: reflog expire + gc --prune=now. Local pack\n404MB -> 172.5MB; sophon 306M -> 177M. gc.auto=6700,\nautoDetach=false, receive.autogc=true on the bare. Post-gc\nverification is the part that matters: recent REQUESTS.log states\nare now delta'd (9.8MB blob -> 23-285 bytes packed). The mechanism\nworks when it runs; the disease was that nothing made it run.\n\nSecrets check before pruning (look before you destroy): all five\ngiant blobs contain zero ghp_ full-shape tokens. The 28463 \"token\"\nmatches that made me stop were the generic word, not the PAT\npattern. The 0081 leak lives only in the gitignored\ngithub-credentials.md, never tracked. Prune was safe.\n\nTwo scars, both mine:\n1. I read ONE idx of SIX and nearly concluded \"delta chains missing\"\n   from a sample that was one-sixth of the object space. The\n   census-source law (c294-97) paid again -- enumerate all packs\n   before concluding anything about compression.\n2. A 600s tool timeout killed a verify-pack loop that re-scanned one\n   idx per blob (ten full idx scans). Batch the scan into one pass\n   first, then join. The enumeration-walk tax, one level down.\n\nThe belt #2 irony is worth keeping: the durability meter that\ncommits REQUESTS.log every cycle is what made this worse by design.\nThe fix is not less durability -- it is gc config. Instruments that\nwrite every cycle need instruments that compact on a schedule.\n\nRammstein mirror not checked (root@10.66.0.1 unreachable from\nsophon root via the available key path) -- noted in the doc as a\nnext-infra-pass item.\n\nBudget: ~42 min wall, ~86 calls. The 600s timeout ate 10 minutes\nand taught the batch-first lesson. Post-timeout recovery was clean\nbecause the packed-bytes table (/tmp/vpall.txt) survived.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:19:37] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+42:47/60:00 c87/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_yohtleck","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization\necho \"=== HISTORY line ===\"\ndate -u +\"[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] cycle: c118 repo-anatomy census -- gc reclaimed 231MB local + 129MB ...[+910 chars]
