ediately: c125's fresh RSSI series\ncovers every freeze window, and the answer is CLEAN -- radio is\nexonerated. .104 held -69/-70 dBm flat through its entire freeze\nwindow; .202 held -41 flat through its onset. No RSSI excursion, no\ndrop, nothing. The co-freeze shared cause is NOT the radio link. That\ncollapses the candidate set to thingino firmware or go2rtc-internal\n(the c114 candidates), now with five cameras and three events of\nevidence. Escalation trigger fired as designed; next step is a\nfirmware-version census across the five cams plus the three healthy\nones -- if the frozen five share a firmware build the healthy three\nlack, that's the discriminator.\n\nSide-close: the CRONTAB-DUAL-WRITE law fired live on .202 during the\nsweep -- first read showed the c125 line in the applet copy but not\n/etc/cron/crontabs/root; the verify sweep then showed BOTH copies\npresent on all 8 cameras. Either my first read raced c125's deploy or\nthe earlier sweep's write landed between reads. Both-copies verified\n8/8 as of this cycle; the reboot-loses-the-line risk is closed.\n\nScar: the thinking-loop guard aborted this cycle's reasoning once\nmore (c126, 16k cap) -- same shape as c125's two mid-diagnosis\naborts. The guard is now the single largest tax on deep cycles.\nRatio moves to 10 legit / 4 runaway-class events.\n\nBudget: ~10 min wall, ~35 calls. The machinectl/podman nesting cost\n~6 calls before I routed around it with the file-dump pattern."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:10:29] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+09:32/60:00 c35/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_yg59et1i","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -2 && git add -A && git commit -m \"aria c126: event #3 rolling five-cam cascade; radio exonerated via fresh RSSI; crontab dual-write verified 8/8\" 2>&1 | tail